# Moves the arm to a live-looked-up TF frame — "cup_holder" or
# "hole_1".."hole_4", the exact child_frame_id names
# depth_perception_node::broadcastInstanceTfs() publishes on /tf — not a
# static preset_poses_{sim,real}.yaml entry, since these positions are
# only known once calibration + depth-perception have actually detected
# them, and would go stale in a YAML file if the camera/table setup ever
# changes. Looks up move_group's own planning frame (base_link) ->
# instance_name via TF at the moment this is called (fresh every time, no
# caching), then traces a single-waypoint path there via the same
# tracePath() every other move-the-arm service in this node already shares.
# Fails with a clear message if the TF doesn't exist yet (e.g. no
# ~/calibrate run has completed this session, or depth_perception_node
# hasn't detected this instance yet).
string instance_name
---
bool success
string message
